      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Old missile bases lie buried in the Overworld and on every planet with solid ground. A complex is about 240 by 240 blocks and 24 blocks down, with a hub, wide halls and hallways branching into 35 to 40 rooms, and a gallery of four to ten real silos. On the surface you see only concrete shafts, sometimes a small radar hut, and an escape-ladder trapdoor. Nothing in a complex is better than its planet\u0027s ceiling: EV in the Overworld and on the Moon, and one voltage tier more for each rocket tier above it. The sign in the Assembly Bay names the class. Guards wait at the posts, and a post you break stays broken. A Data Stick in a Comms chest names the nearest other complex. Find a complex and walk its hall.",
